{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sorry, uh, this computer is still thinking. Take a seat. What brings you in?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Good afternoon, doctor. Thank you for fitting me in. I have come about a lump in the groin.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (DOCTOR): A lump, right. Sorry, say where again, the window jumped.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): The right side, doctor. I am a manual labourer on a building site. When I lift a bag of cement it pushes out, and when I lie down it goes away.",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He's been labouring on that site for years. The bakkie comes home loaded every Friday, I keep telling him.",
  "[SEG0006] person_1 (DOCTOR): Mm. Is it painful?",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (PATIENT): No, doctor. I would not call it pain.",
  "[SEG0008] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any vomiting with it?",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): No. I have not vomited at all.",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): At the desk the sister said my blood pressure was 138 over 84. I thought I ought to mention the figure.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (DOCTOR): 138 over 84. I'll let the note catch up, the screen has frozen. Any cough, or shortness of breath?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): No, doctor. No cough, and I am not short of breath.",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He sleeps badly, though. Shame, he's up and down half the night.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes, that is fair. I have not been sleeping well for some weeks.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sorry, err, the sleep bit again? A pop-up covered the note.",
  "[SEG0016] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He sleeps badly. And he does not take the blood pressure tablets on Sundays.",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (PATIENT): Forgive me, that is not quite accurate. I miss the tablet on Saturdays, not on Sundays. On a Sunday I do take it.",
  "[SEG0018] person_1 (DOCTOR): Which tablet? The font on here is minute.",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (PATIENT): Amlodipine, doctor. Five milligrams, by mouth, every morning, for my blood pressure. I have had the high blood pressure for three years. Saturdays I forget, because I leave for the site so early.",
  "[SEG0020] person_1 (DOCTOR): Amlodipine, five milligrams. The blood pressure is already on your file as an ongoing problem. Say the dose once more, please.",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): Amlodipine, five milligrams, one tablet in the morning.",
  "[SEG0022] person_4 (NURSE): Doctor, sorry to interrupt. The blood pressure I took outside is 138 over 84, and the pulse is 76.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes, sister. That is the same figure I gave a moment ago.",
  "[SEG0024] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ta, sister. Right. How long has this lump been coming out?",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): Six weeks, doctor. It began after a particularly heavy lift.",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): And the cut on his shin, from the scaffold, that healed in five days. Nothing slow about it.",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes, that is correct. It was a small cut and it healed in five days.",
  "[SEG0028] person_1 (DOCTOR): Okay. I lost the thread, one second. You said there was no pain. Is that still right?",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): Well, actually, err, doctor, I should put that properly. By the evening there is a mild ache in the right groin. It is not severe, but it is there after a day's lifting.",
  "[SEG0030] person_1 (DOCTOR): A mild ache by evening. Got it, I think. Are you taking anything for it? Brufen, Panado?",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (PATIENT): I was taking brufin, four hundred milligrams, but I stopped it in March. It was upsetting my stomach.",
  "[SEG0032] person_1 (DOCTOR): Stopped in March. And there's an old script here for tramadol, fifty milligrams. Are you on that?",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (PATIENT): No, doctor. I never took it. They wrote it down and I did not collect it from the chemist.",
  "[SEG0034] person_1 (DOCTOR): Fine, we leave that. Any allergy to medicines?",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (PATIENT): No, doctor. None that I am aware of.",
  "[SEG0036] person_1 (DOCTOR): Do you smoke?",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (PATIENT): No. I have never smoked.",
  "[SEG0038] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): The parking was hectic, hey. And with the load shedding the robot on Main was out, we nearly missed the slot.",
  "[SEG0039] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ja, it's been like that all week. Umm. Hop on the bed for me. Sorry, I must click save or it vanishes.",
  "[SEG0040] person_1 (DOCTOR): There is a soft swelling in the right groin. It reduces when you lie flat, and there is a cough impulse. Your tummy is soft, and it is not tender.",
  "[SEG0041] person_2 (PATIENT): That is exactly where I feel it, doctor.",
  "[SEG0042] person_1 (DOCTOR): This is most likely a right inguinal hernia. That is my working impression. The surgeons will confirm it.",
  "[SEG0043] person_2 (PATIENT): I see. Will I need an operation?",
  "[SEG0044] person_1 (DOCTOR): Quite possibly, but that is their decision. I am referring you to the general surgery clinic, and they will send the booking.",
  "[SEG0045] person_1 (DOCTOR): In the meantime, please do not lift heavy loads. No bags of cement. Ask someone else on the site to take those.",
  "[SEG0046] person_2 (PATIENT): I understand, doctor. I will follow that.",
  "[SEG0047] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): I'll make sure he does. He is stubborn, but he listens if I am there.",
  "[SEG0048] person_1 (DOCTOR): And come back if the lump will not go back in, or if you start vomiting. Do not sit on that.",
  "[SEG0049] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes, doctor. Thank you for explaining it so clearly.",
  "[SEG0050] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Come, we'll beat the queue at the gate. Afternoon, doctor.",
  "[SEG0051] person_1 (DOCTOR): Afternoon. Sister will point you to reception for the referral letter."
 ],
